  Below is a fix to search.c for a memory fault that was occuring
when attempting to search while no weapon was currently wielded.
I am running nethack 3.0h PL6 on a 286 under Xenix 2.3.  Since no
one else has mentioned this searching problem, it may be limited
to the 286 or Xenix 2.3 or the combination.

search.c
92,94c92,93
< 	int fund = 0;
< 	if (uwep && spec_ability(uwep, SPFX_SEARCH))
< 		fund = (uwep->spe > 5) ? 5 : uwep->spe;
---
> 	int fund = (spec_ability(uwep, SPFX_SEARCH)) ?
> 			((uwep->spe > 5) ? 5 : uwep->spe) : 0;

  As i mentioned some time ago, i also had to change the following
lines in termcap.c to prevent core dumps when throwing things.
Because of the nap() calls, i added -lx to the link line.

termcap.c
666c666
< 		nap(50L);
---
> 		tputs("$<50>", 1, (int (*)())xputc);
668c668
< 		nap(50L);
---
> 		tputs("$<50>", 1, xputc);
671c671
< 		nap(50L);
---
> 		tputs("50", 1, xputc);

  On rare and seemingly varying occasions playing PL3 i would get
memory faults in alloc routines.  I haven't been able to narrow
this down yet and i haven't encountered it yet in PL6.  Has anyone
else seen this?

  I have also encountered the pickup bug that someone noted earlier.
Other than these problems, it's a great game.

Thanx.

